After capturing the Enter event with the following code, I dispatched a Click event, triggering the same process as the Click event. Thank you for your answer.

```
    useEffect(() => {
      !isNested &&
        document?.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
          if (event.key === 'Enter') {
            const e = new Event('click', {
              bubbles: true,
              cancelable: true,
            });
            virtualItemRef.current.dispatchEvent(e);
          }
        });
      return () => {
        !isNested &&
          document?.removeEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
            console.log('element keydown', event.key);
          });
      };
    }, []);
```
